From 57d2e955086633821b175ba793b4453ac133c6f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harvey Bellini <harveybellini@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:34:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] S7: pin MCP dependencies and cut credential scope

The MCP tooling forwarded long-lived AWS keys into unpinned ghcr.io images that do not exist publicly, depended on npm 'latest' specs (including @zetalytics/mcp-google-calendar, which is not published), and left the installed Playwright config on approval mode auto. npm servers are now pinned to exact versions with refreshed lockfiles, the AWS servers use digest-pinned public ECR images with a read-only ~/.aws mount and AWS_PROFILE, the Google Calendar server moves to the pinned upstream package with OAuth credentials, docs state minimum scopes, and scripts/refresh-mcp-pins.ps1 plus a test keep the pins honest. The installed .codex/config.toml must be regenerated by re-running scripts/install-mcps.ps1 (sandbox is read-only there).
